  "caption": "Quinn's new running route seemed cursed: at the same spot every run, the shins went tight, full and a little numb, then felt fine after a few minutes' rest.\n\nPain that builds predictably with running and settles quickly at rest may not be classic shin splints. In some people the muscles swell inside a snug compartment and pressure rises until they stop.\n\nWhat often helps: interval-style running below the point where symptoms start, gait retraining such as quicker, shorter steps and a softer landing, reviewing shoes and recent training load, and building calf capacity.\n\nDon't push through numbness or weakness, and get it checked. Sudden severe pain after a knock is an emergency, so call 000.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
